course: dictionary
lesson: 7843
title: Rad and other slang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a group of people, a place, or a time. «Rad» is slang, a fun informal word that means really cool or great. You will hear it in «That skateboard trick was rad!» or «That's rad». When you meet a word like this, look at the words around it: a skateboard trick that looks amazing makes rad mean awesome.
explain: Context can also show you how old a word is. Some slang sounds a bit retro now, like something from an old cartoon or from grandad's day. In a bicycle sentence, Amara's mum says the bikes are «proper rad», and they gave women the freedom to travel on their own. So rad means really cool, and she says it with pride.
explain: Rad can mean other things, but only in special places. In maths, rad is short for radian, a unit for measuring angles, and in science a rad is an old unit for measuring radiation. You will meet these later in secondary school. In British talk, a rad can be short for a radiator, the thing on the wall that heats a room.
fact: Rad is an informal word that means really cool or great.
fact: «Totally rad» and «that's rad» are ways people say that something is awesome.
fact: «Rad» sounds a bit old-fashioned now, and in the US it is older slang for great.
fact: In maths, rad is short for radian, an angle unit; in science, a rad is an old unit for radiation.
fact: In British talk, a rad can be short for a radiator, which heats a room.
exercise: «That skateboard trick was rad!» What does rad mean here? | A small, sad animal | Slow and quiet | *Really cool | Very wet and grey
exercise: In maths, rad is short for which word? | Radar | Radiator | *Radian | Radio
exercise: Amara's mum says her bicycles are «proper rad». Why does she say it? | Because the bicycles are rusty and old | Because they heat the room | Because she is cross with the bicycles | *Because they gave women the freedom to travel on their own
test: What does «that's rad» mean? | Really sad | *Really cool | Really wet | Really small
test: A character in a story says «Rad, dude!» What kind of character is this? | A tired, grumpy character | A very angry character | *A cool, casual character | A lost character
exam: Read «Totally rad, Sam!» and use the context to choose the meaning of rad. | Angry | *Awesome | Frozen | Sleepy
